<title>PERU: Peru state miner Centromin gives workers pay rise.</title>
<headline>Peru state miner Centromin gives workers pay rise.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's state miner Centromin said Friday it had agreed on a workers' pay rise with the seven unions that represent the company's 6,590 blue-collar employees.</p>
<p>Workers will receive an average of an extra 4.20 soles ($1.70) per day to take their average monthly wage to 1,054 soles, the company announced.</p>
<p>Centromin is in the midst of a piecemeal privatization to sell its seven mines, its La Oroya metallurgical complex, a railroad network, port facilities, four hydroelectric plants and several prospects.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
